<!-- ============ WHO IT IS FOR ============ -->
<section class="ac-blue sunk section">
  <div class="container">
    <div class="section-header">
      <div class="section-eyebrow">Cloud Back Office · In Practice</div>
      <h2 class="section-title">One source of truth, four different questions.</h2>
      <p class="section-sub">The value of a dashboard is not the chart. It is that the person who has to act can reach the cause themselves, without filing a request and waiting two days for an answer that has already gone stale.</p>
    </div>
    <div class="intx-grid intx-grid-2">
      <div class="intx-item">
        <span class="intx-n">01</span>
        <h3>Retail leadership</h3>
        <p>Performance arrives fragmented across stores, e-commerce and the warehouse. Here it is one view, and it drills: a margin number that looks wrong opens into the locations behind it, then the items, then the receipt itself.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="intx-item">
        <span class="intx-n">02</span>
        <h3>Merchandising and planning</h3>
        <p>Stockouts on one side, markdowns on the other. Stock on hand sits next to RFM customer segmentation, and the 4-5-4 retail calendar is native, so week-over-week and year-over-year land correctly without a spreadsheet and a VLOOKUP.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="intx-item">
        <span class="intx-n">03</span>
        <h3>Store and district operations</h3>
        <p>District managers lose their mornings rebuilding the same store report. Instead the sales and stock summary is delivered by email as a PDF, CSV or Excel file on a set schedule, waiting before the doors open.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="intx-item">
        <span class="intx-n">04</span>
        <h3>IT and data</h3>
        <p>The usual trade-off is that reporting queries slow the tills at the worst possible moment. Analytics run on a dedicated Google BigQuery backend, decoupled from the operational database, so querying years of transactions never touches checkout speed on Black Friday.</p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

